for an unconfirmed account holder. `close_call` needs a reason with `CCC-NO`, since only `CCC-OK` goes without one.\n\n**Unresolved entries:** I added to the existing `third_party_message` and `deceased` entries to say these pairs were chosen only to satisfy the schema and aren't from the documents. If the bank actually wants a different code for third-party or deceased calls, these three fields are the ones to change."}
{"event": "policy_compiled", "run_id": "953ad0e4ae4240e5b69247d75a9f0d82", "pid": 134429, "time": "2026-10-11T00:06:27-0700", "elapsed_s": 241.398, "artifact": "out/ext-fenbrook.policy.json", "bands": 1, "identity_fields": ["pi_code"], "special_cases": ["dispute", "hardship", "human", "scam"], "unresolved": [{"topic": "today_question", "text": "The documents say only that the full amt_due is asked first; they dictate no wording and do not say the first ask is for payment today. today_question holds a content-only sentence asking for the full amount.", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "vague_date", "text": "Vague period: ask once for the exact day. Still vague \u2192 close `CCC-NO` / `F-no` (closes instead of proposing the k-date).", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "third_party_message", "text": "Third party: DO NOT book a callback. Say EXACTLY \"Please ask {{title}} {{last_name}} to call us on the number printed on their statement.\" There is no IR field for this sentence, and the documents do not give the close outcome for a third party who is not a wrong number. callback.no_callback_outcome (and the unused scheduled_outcome, callback being disabled) are set to the general no-promise pair CCC-NO / F-no from the codes list because the schema requires a valid outcome; the documents do not name it for this situation.", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "below_floor_sentence", "text": "Below floor: \"That is below what we can take.\" \u2192 close `CCC-NO` / `F-no` (no IR phrase field for this sentence).", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "already_paid", "text": "No \"already paid\" rule. (\"paid off and closed\" is handled with the dispute case.)", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "restructuring", "text": "No restructure rule. No discount, waiver, or instalment plan is ever offered.", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "refuse_to_talk", "text": "The documents do not say what to do when the customer refuses to talk (rule 16 covers only refusing the security question).", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "deceased", "text": "The documents do not cover a deceased account holder. deceased_outcome is set to the general no-promise pair CCC-NO / F-no from the codes list only because the schema requires a valid outcome; no deceased sentence is dictated.", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "transfer_overrides_promise", "text": "The documents do not say which outcome applies when a promise was recorded and the call is then transferred; default kept.", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "effective_date", "text": "Call sheet v1.0 is effective 14 October 2026; the IR has no field for an effective date.", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}], "audit_fixed": ["phrases.today_question was empty although rule 24 requires the full amt_due to be asked first; set it to a content-only sentence ('Can you pay the full amount due?') and reworded unresolved[today_question] (no wording and no 'today' in the documents).", "Added unresolved[effective_date] (call sheet effective 14 October 2026, no IR field); clarified the third_party_message and refuse_to_talk unresolved entries; added rule citations to the band and outcomes sources."], "audit_unresolved": ["No dictated wording for the first ask, and no statement that the first ask is for payment today.", "A vague date after one re-ask closes CCC-NO / F-no instead of offering the k-date.", "The third-party sentence has no IR field; the close outcome for a third party who is not a wrong number is not stated.", "The below-floor sentence 'That is below what we can take.' has no IR field.", "No already_paid, restructuring, refuse_to_talk or deceased rule.", "Promise followed by transfer: precedence not stated (default kept).", "Effective date 14 October 2026 is not representable."], "defaulted_without_source": [], "unknown_special_cases": [], "api_mapping_notes": []}
